{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/afluent\/asyncsequences\/timeout\/broadcast()"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent","doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences","doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/Timeout"]]},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns a sequence that multicasts elements to multiple concurrent consumers."}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/Timeout\/broadcast()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"broadcast","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent22AsyncBroadcastSequenceV","text":"AsyncBroadcastSequence","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncBroadcastSequence"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Return Value","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"return-value"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"code":"AsyncBroadcastSequence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that multicasts elements to multiple consumers concurrently.","type":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This operator enables multicasting of values from the upstream sequence to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"multiple consumers that iterate concurrently. Each consumer sees the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sequence of elements, and elements are only fetched once from the upstream"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sequence."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"broadcast","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" creates a new shared sequence that manages buffering and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"distribution of elements to all active iterators. A consumer receives the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements the shared sequence reads from the upstream after the consumer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"creates its iterator; elements already read and handed out are not replayed."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"code":"broadcast","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"share","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" operators are functionally equivalent and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can be used interchangeably."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Example","type":"heading","text":"Example"},{"code":["\/\/ Create an AsyncStream that emits 3 random values between 1 and 5","let upstream = AsyncStream<Int> { continuation in","    continuation.yield(Int.random(in: 1...5))","    continuation.yield(Int.random(in: 1...5))","    continuation.yield(Int.random(in: 1...5))","    continuation.finish()","}","","let sharedSequence = upstream.broadcast()","","async let firstConsumer = Task {","    for await value in sharedSequence {","        print(\"First consumer received \\(value)\")","    }","    \/\/ prints the values the shared sequence reads after this consumer subscribed","}","","async let secondConsumer = Task {","    for await value in sharedSequence {","        print(\"Second consumer received \\(value)\")","    }","    \/\/ prints the values the shared sequence reads after this consumer subscribed","}","","\/\/ A consumer that subscribes after the shared sequence has handed out values misses them.","await firstConsumer.value","await secondConsumer.value"],"type":"codeListing","synta